---
import "./terms.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index,follow" />

    <title>Cookie Policy — ViralMMSVideo</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="./terms.css" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <!-- Fixed Navigation -->
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="nav-inner">
        <button
          class="back-button"
          type="button"
          onclick="history.back()"
          aria-label="Go back"
          title="Go back"
        >
          <span aria-hidden="true">←</span>
        </button>

        <a href="/" class="brand">ViralMMSVideo</a>

        <nav class="main-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy</a>
          <a href="/dmca-policy.html">DMCA</a>
          <a href="/terms.html">Terms</a>
          <a href="/report-abuse.html">Report Abuse</a>
          <a href="/content-safety.html">Content Safety</a>
          <a href="/cookie-policy.html" class="active">Cookies</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="page-shell">
      <section class="page-header">
        <div class="eyebrow">LEGAL DOCUMENT</div>

        <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>

        <p class="page-description">
          Information about cookies, similar technologies, their purposes, and
          how you can manage them.
        </p>

        <div class="last-updated">Last Updated: August 20, 2026</div>
      </section>

      <div class="content-layout">
        <!-- Table of Contents -->
        <aside class="toc-wrapper">
          <div class="toc-card">
            <div class="toc-title">Table of Contents</div>

            <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of Contents">
              <a href="#what">1. What Are Cookies?</a>
              <a href="#use">2. How We Use Cookies</a>
              <a href="#types">3. Types of Cookies</a>
              <a href="#essential">4. Essential Cookies</a>
              <a href="#analytics">5. Analytics</a>
              <a href="#third-party">6. Third-Party Technologies</a>
              <a href="#manage">7. Managing Cookies</a>
              <a href="#retention">8. Cookie Duration</a>
              <a href="#changes">9. Changes to This Policy</a>
              <a href="#contact">10. Contact</a>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <!-- Main Policy -->
        <article class="policy-card">
          <div class="notice">
            This Cookie Policy explains how ViralMMSVideo may use cookies and
            similar technologies when you visit or use the Platform.
          </div>

          <section id="what">
            <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>

            <p>
              Cookies are small text files or similar identifiers that may be
              stored on your device when you visit a website.
            </p>

            <p>
              Cookies can help websites remember information, maintain sessions,
              understand how visitors use a service, and support certain
              functionality.
            </p>

            <p>
              Similar technologies may include local storage, pixels, tags,
              scripts, or other identifiers that perform functions comparable to
              cookies.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="use">
            <h2>2. How We Use Cookies</h2>

            <p>
              Depending on how the Platform is configured, cookies or similar
              technologies may be used to:
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>keep the website functioning correctly;</li>
              <li>maintain security and prevent abuse;</li>
              <li>remember certain preferences or settings;</li>
              <li>understand website usage and performance;</li>
              <li>measure traffic and improve the Platform; and</li>
              <li>support services provided by authorized third parties.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              We do not claim that every cookie or similar technology is used
              for every purpose listed above at all times.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="types">
            <h2>3. Types of Cookies</h2>

            <p>
              Cookies may generally be grouped into the following categories:
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Essential cookies:</strong>
                necessary for core website functionality, security, or session management.
              </li>

              <li>
                <strong>Preference cookies:</strong>
                used to remember settings or choices where applicable.
              </li>

              <li>
                <strong>Analytics cookies:</strong>
                used to understand traffic, usage, and website performance.
              </li>

              <li>
                <strong>Third-party cookies:</strong>
                cookies or similar technologies placed or controlled by third-party
                services used by the Platform.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              The exact technologies used may change as the Platform,
              infrastructure, or third-party services change.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="essential">
            <h2>4. Essential Cookies</h2>

            <p>
              Some cookies may be necessary for the Platform to operate
              correctly. These may support functions such as security,
              authentication, session management, load balancing, or basic
              website operation.
            </p>

            <p>
              Blocking or deleting essential cookies may cause some parts of the
              Platform to stop working correctly.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="analytics">
            <h2>5. Analytics</h2>

            <p>
              Where analytics services are enabled, cookies or similar
              technologies may be used to help understand how visitors interact
              with the Platform.
            </p>

            <p>
              Analytics information may help us understand traffic patterns,
              identify technical problems, measure performance, and improve
              website functionality.
            </p>

            <p>
              Analytics services, if used, may be operated by third-party
              providers and may process information according to their own
              privacy policies.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="third-party">
            <h2>6. Third-Party Technologies</h2>

            <p>
              Some pages or services may use third-party technologies that place
              or access cookies or similar identifiers.
            </p>

            <p>
              Examples may include hosting, security, analytics, content
              delivery, advertising, embedded media, or other service providers,
              depending on the Platform configuration.
            </p>

            <p>
              Third-party services may have their own policies governing their
              use of cookies and similar technologies. We recommend reviewing
              the applicable third-party privacy and cookie documentation where
              relevant.
            </p>

            <div class="notice">
              The exact list of third-party providers and technologies may
              change over time. This policy therefore describes categories and
              purposes rather than guaranteeing a fixed list of providers.
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="manage">
            <h2>7. Managing Cookies</h2>

            <p>
              Most modern web browsers allow you to view, block, delete, or
              restrict cookies through browser settings.
            </p>

            <p>
              You can generally manage cookie settings through your browser's
              privacy, security, or site-settings controls.
            </p>

            <p>
              If you disable cookies, some Platform features may not function
              properly, particularly features that depend on essential cookies.
            </p>

            <p>
              Deleting cookies does not necessarily prevent all forms of
              information collection by websites or third-party services.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="retention">
            <h2>8. Cookie Duration</h2>

            <p>Cookies may be either:</p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Session cookies</strong>, which are generally removed
                when your browser session ends; or
              </li>

              <li>
                <strong>Persistent cookies</strong>, which remain on your device
                for a defined period or until they are deleted.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              The duration of a particular cookie depends on its purpose,
              configuration, and the service that sets it.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="changes">
            <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>

            <p>
              We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect
              changes to the Platform, technologies, legal requirements, or
              operational practices.
            </p>

            <p>
              The updated version will be published on the Platform with a
              revised "Last Updated" date.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="contact">
            <h2>10. Contact</h2>

            <p>
              If you have questions about cookies, privacy, or the handling of
              information on the Platform, contact:
            </p>

            <p>
              <a href="mailto:support@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org">
                <strong>support@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org</strong>
              </a>
            </p>

            <p>For copyright complaints, please use:</p>

            <p>
              <a href="mailto:dmca@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org">
                <strong>dmca@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org</strong>
              </a>
            </p>

            <div class="notice">
              This Cookie Policy is a general description of cookie and similar
              technology practices. Cookie requirements and privacy rights can
              vary by jurisdiction and may change over time.
            </div>
          </section>

          <footer class="policy-footer">
            <p>© 2026 ViralMMSVideo. All rights reserved.</p>

            <nav class="footer-links">
              <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
              <a href="/dmca-policy">DMCA Policy</a>
              <a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>
              <a href="/report-abuse">Report Abuse</a>
              <a href="/content-safety">Content Safety</a>
              <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>
            </nav>
          </footer>
        </article>
      </div>
    </main>

    <!-- Back to Top -->
    <button
      class="top-button"
      type="button"
      aria-label="Back to top"
      title="Back to top"
      onclick="window.scrollTo({top: 0, behavior: 'smooth'})"
    >
      ↑
    </button>
  </body>
</html>
